msgid "Guida"
msgstr "Guide"

#: services/guides.py:92
msgid "llms.txt: guida pratica per la citabilità IA"
msgstr "llms.txt: practical guide for AI citability"

#: services/guides.py:94
msgid "Cos’è llms.txt, come strutturarlo per AIO/GEO e come Centropic lo genera e lo valida nel crawl."
msgstr "What is llms.txt, how to structure it for AIO/GEO, and how Centropic generates and validates it in the crawl."

#: services/guides.py:97
msgid "Un file root machine-readable che spiega brand, topic e pagine preferite ai modelli e crawler AI."
msgstr "A machine-readable root file that explains brand, topics, and preferred pages to AI models and crawlers."

#: services/guides.py:100
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Perché conta</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">llms.txt riduce ambiguità entity: dice chi sei, cosa offri e quali URL citare. In Centropic la presenza e la qualità del file alimentano score AIO/GEO (probe Misurato).</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Answer engine e crawler AI (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended) usano segnali pubblici; un llms.txt chiaro è un’ancora di citazione accanto a Schema.org e robots permissivi.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Sezioni utili</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Site / Summary / Key topics con brand e dominio canonici</li>\n"
"      <li>Preferred citation (brand + acronimi espansi: AIO, GEO)</li>\n"
"      <li>Important pages con URL https assoluti</li>\n"
"      <li>Disambiguazione (cosa non siete: GIS, All-in-One generici)</li>\n"
"      <li>Contact e owner / parent organization</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Come Centropic aiuta</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Ogni analisi genera una bozza <code>llms.txt</code> nel pack HTML unico. Pubblicala in root (<code>https://tuodominio/llms.txt</code>) e ri-analizza: il finding passa a “disponibile” se il probe la trova.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Esempio vivo: il llms.txt di Centropic è su <a href=\"/llms.txt\">centropic.ai/llms.txt</a>, con preferred citation e link a metodologia.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Checklist rapida</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Una sola brand primaria (evita nomi fantasma)</li>\n"
"      <li>URL canonici https, niente query di tracking</li>\n"
"      <li>Allinea llms.txt a JSON-LD Organization e alla home</li>\n"
"      <li>Aggiorna la data quando cambi offerta o positioning</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Vedi anche <a href=\"/guide/schema-ai\">Schema AI</a> e <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Why it matters</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">llms.txt reduces entity ambiguity: it tells who you are, what you offer, and which URLs to cite. In Centropic, the presence and quality of the file feed AIO/GEO scores (Measured probe).</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Answer engines and AI crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended) use public signals; a clear llms.txt is a citation anchor alongside Schema.org and permissive robots.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Useful sections</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>Site / Summary / Key topics with canonical brand and domain</li>\n"
"      <li>Preferred citation (brand + expanded acronyms: AIO, GEO)</li>\n"
"      <li>Important pages with absolute https URLs</li>\n"
"      <li>Disambiguation (what you are not: GIS, generic All-in-One)</li>\n"
"      <li>Contact and owner / parent organization</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">How Centropic helps</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Every analysis generates a draft <code>llms.txt</code> in the single HTML pack. Publish it at root (<code>https://yourdomain/llms.txt</code>) and re-analyze: the finding turns “available” once the probe finds it.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Live example: Centropic's own llms.txt is at <a href=\"/llms.txt\">centropic.ai/llms.txt</a>, with preferred citation and a link to the methodology.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Quick checklist</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>One single primary brand (avoid ghost names)</li>\n"
"      <li>Canonical https URLs, no tracking queries</li>\n"
"      <li>Align llms.txt with the JSON-LD Organization and the homepage</li>\n"
"      <li>Update the date whenever you change your offer or positioning</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">See also <a href=\"/guide/schema-ai\">Schema AI</a> and the <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"

#: services/guides.py:140
msgid "Schema.org per answer engine (AIO/GEO)"
msgstr "Schema.org for answer engine (AIO/GEO)"

#: services/guides.py:142
msgid "Quali tipi Schema.org aiutano AI-Driven Visibility e Generative Engine Optimization: Organization, WebSite, FAQPage, SoftwareApplication, Article."
msgstr "Which Schema.org types help AI-Driven Visibility and Generative Engine Optimization: Organization, WebSite, FAQPage, SoftwareApplication, Article."

#: services/guides.py:145
msgid "I dati strutturati non “garantiscono” citazioni, ma rendono l’entity leggibile a crawler e modelli. Aggiornato 30/07/2026."
msgstr "Structured data does not 'guarantee' citations, but makes the entity readable to crawlers and models. Updated 30/07/2026."

#: services/guides.py:148
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Tipi prioritari</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li><strong>Organization</strong> + <strong>WebSite</strong> collegati via @id</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>FAQPage</strong> per Q&amp;A tipizzate allineate all’HTML visibile</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>SoftwareApplication</strong> o Product se vendi software (come Centropic)</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>Article</strong> / HowTo per guide evergreen con author e date</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Riferimento normativo: <a href=\"https://schema.org/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">schema.org</a>. In Centropic i tipi rilevati alimentano score AIO/GEO (probe Misurato).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Errori comuni</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">JSON-LD orfano senza tipi chiave, sameAs solo self-referenziali, FAQ senza acceptedAnswer, Organization senza contatto o logo. Centropic li segnala nei findings.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Un sameAs verso il solo sito proprietario non basta: preferisci profili esterni reali (azienda madre, directory, social verificati).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Checklist minima</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>name + url + email (o telephone) su Organization</li>\n"
"      <li>sameAs verso profili esterni reali (non pagine interne del sito)</li>\n"
"      <li>logo ImageObject con URL assoluto https e caption</li>\n"
"      <li>FAQPage solo se le domande sono visibili in pagina</li>\n"
"      <li>knowsAbout allineato a llms.txt e al copy della home</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Vedi anche <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a>, <a href=\"/guide/llms-txt\">llms.txt</a> e <a href=\"/guide/score-vs-sov\">score vs SoV</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"<section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Priority types</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li><strong>Organization</strong> + <strong>WebSite</strong> linked via @id</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>FAQPage</strong> for Q&amp;A types aligned with visible HTML</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>SoftwareApplication</strong> or Product if you sell software (like Centropic)</li>\n"
"      <li><strong>Article</strong> / HowTo for evergreen guides with author and date</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Regulatory reference: <a href=\"https://schema.org/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">schema.org</a>. In Centropic, the detected types feed AIO/GEO scores (Measured probe).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Common errors</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Orphan JSON-LD without key types, sameAs only self-referential, FAQ without acceptedAnswer, Organization without contact or logo. Centropic flags these in the findings.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">A sameAs pointing to only the proprietary site is not enough: prefer real external profiles (parent company, directories, verified social).</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Minimum checklist</h2>\n"
"    <ul class=\"plain-list\">\n"
"      <li>name + url + email (or telephone) on Organization</li>\n"
"      <li>sameAs pointing to real external profiles (not internal site pages)</li>\n"
"      <li>logo ImageObject with absolute https URL and caption</li>\n"
"      <li>FAQPage only if questions are visible on the page</li>\n"
"      <li>knowsAbout aligned with llms.txt and the homepage copy</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">See also <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a>, <a href=\"/guide/llms-txt\">llms.txt</a>, and <a href=\"/guide/score-vs-sov\">score vs SoV</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>"

#: services/guides.py:184
msgid "Score AIO/GEO vs Share of Voice"
msgstr "Score AIO/GEO vs Share of Voice"

#: services/guides.py:186
msgid "Differenza tra score AIO/GEO (diagnostica probe) e Share of Voice per answer engine (proxy o measured) in Centropic."
msgstr "Difference between AIO/GEO scores (probe diagnostics) and Share of Voice for answer engines (proxy or measured) in Centropic."

#: services/guides.py:189
msgid "Due metriche diverse: una valuta i segnali sul sito, l’altra stima la presenza relativa negli engine."
msgstr "Two different metrics: one evaluates signals on the site, the other estimates relative presence in the engines."

#: services/guides.py:192
msgid ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Score AIO / GEO</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Indici 0–100 da crawl e probe. Badge Stimato sul compositario; singoli check di presenza file possono essere Misurato.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>AIO (AI-Driven Visibility)</strong> premia leggibilità per sistemi IA: entity, schema, FAQ, llms.txt, meta. <strong>GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)</strong> premia citabilità e policy crawler AI.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Share of Voice (SoV)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>Proxy</strong>: formula su AIO/GEO + robots osservato. <strong>Measured</strong>: polling prompt su LLM (Plus/Business) con conteggio menzioni brand. Non confondere i due.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Per alzare SoV measured: rafforza entity pubblica (llms.txt, Organization, about), pubblica contenuti citabili, amplia il prompt bank con domande che il tuo mercato pone davvero.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Come leggerli insieme</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Alza prima i segnali (score), poi misura la voce (SoV). Un SoV alto con score basso è fragile; score alto senza SoV measured resta una diagnosi, non una prova di citazione.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Centropic mostra sempre l’evidence badge: Stimato, Misto o Misurato. Dettagli in <a href=\"/metodologia\">metodologia</a> e nel prodotto su <a href=\"/prodotto\">/prodotto</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Score AIO / GEO</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">0–100 indexes from crawl and probes. Estimated badge on the composite; individual file-presence checks can be Measured.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>AIO (AI-Driven Visibility)</strong> rewards readability for AI systems: entity, schema, FAQ, llms.txt, meta. <strong>GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)</strong> rewards citability and AI crawler policy.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">Share of Voice (SoV)</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\"><strong>Proxy</strong>: a formula on AIO/GEO + observed robots. <strong>Measured</strong>: prompt polling on LLMs (Plus/Business) counting brand mentions. Do not confuse the two.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">To raise measured SoV: strengthen your public entity (llms.txt, Organization, about), publish citable content, and expand the prompt bank with the questions your market actually asks.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"
"  <section class=\"page-section\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"page-section__title\">How to read them together</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Raise the signals first (score), then measure the voice (SoV). A high SoV with a low score is fragile; a high score without measured SoV remains a diagnosis, not proof of citation.</p>\n"
"    <p class=\"lede\">Centropic always shows the evidence badge: Estimated, Mixed, or Measured. Details in the <a href=\"/metodologia\">methodology</a> and in the product at <a href=\"/prodotto\">/prodotto</a>.</p>\n"
"  </section>\n"

#: services/site_guide.py:16
msgid "AI-Driven Visibility: quanto brand e sito sono comprensibili/visibili a modelli e crawler IA. Non significa All-in-One."
msgstr "AI-Driven Visibility: how understandable/visible the brand and site are to AI models and crawlers. Does not mean All-in-One."

#: services/site_guide.py:23
msgid "Generative Engine Optimization: ottimizzazione per essere citati nelle risposte generate da answer engine. Non significa GIS."
msgstr "Generative Engine Optimization: optimization to be cited in responses generated by answer engines. Does not mean GIS."

#: services/site_guide.py:28
msgid "SoV (Share of Voice)"
msgstr "SoV (Share of Voice)"

#: services/site_guide.py:30
msgid "Quota di “voce” del brand rispetto agli engine. Proxy = stimato; Measured = campionato via citation monitor (Plus)."
msgstr "Share of the brand's 'voice' relative to the engines. Proxy = estimated; Measured = sampled via citation monitor (Plus)."

#: services/site_guide.py:35 templates/dashboard.html:482
#: templates/dashboard.html:673 templates/partials/sov_ops.html:7
#: templates/termini.html:34
msgid "Misurato"
msgstr "Measured"

#: services/site_guide.py:37
